<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Halla Group plans German pulp venture.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Halla Group plans German pulp venture.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Halla Group said on Monday it had signed a memorandum of understanding with Germany's Harpen AG to build a pulp plant in Zeitz, eastern Germany.</p>
<p>The pulp plant, which will have a production capacity of 500,000 tonnes a year, is due to start operation in March, 2000, a Halla statement said. The two firms were now looking for a third German partner to join the project, it added.</p>
<p>Details, including the value of investment, are still being negotiated between Halla and Harpen AG, it said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
